==Relationships and marriage==
===Bachelorhood===

===Qümica===
[[File:Bacha_XVIII_and_Qümica_in_2400.jpg|250px|thumb|right|Bacha and [[Queen Qümica of Qym|Qümica]] in {{abbr|2400|1994 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}]]
Bacha first met [[Queen Qümica of Qym|Qümica]] through mutual friends in {{abbr|2399|1993 (Earth Year Equivalent)}} when he was {{abbr|34|28 (Earth Age Equivalent)}} and she was {{abbr|30|25 (Earth Age Equivalent)}}. They started dating officially in {{abbr|2400|1994 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, attracting intense attention from the press and paparazzi. Comparisons with his father [[Bacha XVII of Qym|Bacha XVII]]'s relationship with his mother, [[Queen Zvonica of Qym|Queen Zvonica]] were also common. The couple was described as having great chemistry and a "loving demeanor" suggesting reciprocal affection. However, as years went by and the couple delayed marriage, speculation mounted and scrutiny on Qümica's character emerged. In {{abbr|2403|1996 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, during a television interview, Bacha stated they were in "no rush to marry" and were still "getting to know each other fully". In {{abbr|2404|1997 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, the tabloid [[NEWSPAPER]] published a story going over various hypotheses, from suggesting Bacha's impotence or Qümica's infertility to alleging Qümica's infidelity and poor character. The Crown sued the NEWSPAPER for defamation and spreading misinformation, winning the controversial court case later in {{abbr|2404|1997 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. Shortly after the court case, Qümica did a television interview where she explained her views on her relationship with Bacha, notably stating she needed to "make sure he was the right man" for her, jokingly adding that "[[wikipedia:Prince Charming|Prince Charming]] is not always as he seems," referring to usual portrayals of that stock character archetype as narcissistic, dimwitted, and solely focused on romance, and often as a foil to either the heroine or their true love interest. When pressed on characterizing Bacha's personality in comparison, Qümica poked fun at her boyfriend, describing him as a "not-so-charming prince" and "a man who usually talks too much, but also knows when to keep quiet and appreciate a moment," concluding that he was "alright, but could improve, a bit like this country". Following this interview and the court case, media attention was markedly more positive and Qümica's popularity increased drastically. According to political commentator [[Marlo Birval]], Qümica's description of Bacha helped humanizing the royal couple and portray them as relatable to the commoners. 

After {{abbr|8 years|6 years (Earth Year Equivalent)}} of dating, Bacha married [[Queen Qümica of Qym|Qümica]] on # MONTH {{abbr|2408|2000 (Earth Year Equivalent)}} in [[Zhol]], in a civil ceremony at the [[Zhol City Hall]] and a religious ceremony at the [[Palace of Zhifol]] in [[Zhifol]]. They have four children who were all born at [[NAME Hospital]] in [[BOROUGH]], Zhol:

